-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"9273\" data-servings=\"6\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Fruits</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">strawberries, hulled and halved</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">green grapes, washed</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">pineapple chunks, fresh or canned</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">honeydew melon, cubed</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">marshmallows, mini or regular</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-9273-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9273\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">6 wooden skewers&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For assembling the kabobs</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-9273-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-9273-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9273\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9273-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Start by washing all your fruit thoroughly. This includes strawberries, grapes, pineapple, and melon. Make sure they are clean and ready to go!</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Cutting</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9273-step-1-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Next, cut your pineapple and melon into bite-sized pieces. Aim for uniform sizes so they thread easily onto the skewers. This will make your kabobs look extra appealing!</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Assembling</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9273-step-2-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Now, grab your skewers! Thread the fruit and marshmallows alternately onto the skewers. Create a fun red, green, and white pattern. Get creative with the arrangement!</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Chilling</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9273-step-3-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Finally, place your assembled kabobs in the fridge for about 30 minutes. This chilling time helps the flavors meld and makes them refreshing to eat!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-9273-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>0.5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>1g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbohydrates</td>\n<td>36g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sugar</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these vibrant ingredients to create your festive Christmas fruit kabobs!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Festive-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-1.webp\" alt=\"Colorful Christmas fruit kabobs on a rustic kitchen table with strawberries, grapes, pineapple, melon, and marshmallows.\" class=\"wp-image-9271\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Festive-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-1.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Festive-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-1-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – strawberries, hulled and halved</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – green grapes, washed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – pineapple chunks, fresh or canned</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – honeydew melon, cubed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – marshmallows, mini or regular</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>6</strong> – wooden skewers, for assembling</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-christmas-fruit-kabobs\"><strong>How to Make Christmas Fruit Kabobs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to create a festive treat that’s as fun to make as it is to eat! This Christmas fruit kabobs recipe is perfect for holiday gatherings. With a preparation time of about 15 minutes and no cooking time, you can whip these up quickly. Just remember to chill them for about 30 minutes before serving for the best flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of Christmas fruit kabobs, showcasing washing, cutting, assembling, and chilling the fruit skewers.\" class=\"wp-image-9272\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Christmas-Fruit-Kabobs-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Wash and Prepare Fruit</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by washing all your fruit thoroughly. This includes strawberries, grapes, pineapple, and melon. Make sure they are clean and ready to go!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Cut Pineapple and Melon</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Next, cut your pineapple and melon into bite-sized pieces. Aim for uniform sizes so they thread easily onto the skewers. This will make your kabobs look extra appealing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Thread Fruit and Marshmallows</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now, grab your skewers! Thread the fruit and marshmallows alternately onto the skewers. Create a fun red, green, and white pattern. Get creative with the arrangement!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Chill Before Serving</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finally, place your assembled kabobs in the fridge for about 30 minutes. This chilling time helps the flavors meld and makes them refreshing to eat!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>30 minutes (chilling)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Chilled and refreshing!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-christmas-fruit-kabobs\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Christmas Fruit Kabobs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose a variety of colorful fruits for a festive look.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Soak wooden skewers in water to prevent burning on the grill.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in some marshmallows for a fun texture contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let kids help with assembling for a family-friendly activity.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with honey or yogurt for added flavor before serving.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-christmas-fruit-kabobs\"><strong>How to Serve this Christmas fruit kabobs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve on a festive platter for a colorful centerpiece.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a yogurt dip or chocolate sauce for extra indulgence.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include a mix of seasonal fruits like pomegranate and kiwi for variety.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use mini marshmallows or coconut flakes for added texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Perfect for holiday parties or as a fun snack for kids.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh mint leaves for a pop of color.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your Christmas fruit kabobs fresh and delicious:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Place leftovers in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate within two hours of serving.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consume within 2-3 days for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Christmas Fruit Kabobs</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap each kabob tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped kabobs in a freezer-safe bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Christmas Fruit Kabobs</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve cold for the best taste and texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>If desired, briefly warm in the microwave for 10-15 seconds.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What&#8217;s the best fruit to use in winter kabobs?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For winter kabobs, fruits like apples, pears, oranges, and pomegranates are excellent choices. They not only add vibrant colors but also provide a refreshing taste that complements the holiday spirit. You can also include seasonal fruits like cranberries for a festive touch!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Can I prepare fruit skewers the night before?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Preparing fruit skewers the night before can save you time on the day of your event. Just make sure to store them in an airtight container in the refrigerator to keep the fruit fresh and prevent browning. You can also drizzle a little lemon juice on fruits like apples and pears to help maintain their color!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What fruit is best on a skewer?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Fruits that are firm and hold their shape well are best for skewers. Some great options include strawberries, grapes, melon, and pineapple. These fruits are not only delicious but also easy to thread onto skewers, making them perfect for your Christmas fruit kabobs!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Do you need to soak skewers for fruit kebabs?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>If you&#8217;re using wooden skewers, it&#8217;s a good idea to soak them in water for about 30 minutes before using them. This helps prevent the skewers from burning if you&#8217;re grilling them. However, if you&#8217;re using metal skewers, soaking isn&#8217;t necessary. Just make sure to handle them carefully as they can get hot!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These Christmas fruit kabobs are not just a treat; they’re a delightful way to spread holiday cheer! With their vibrant colors and fresh flavors, they’re sure to bring smiles to your gatherings. So grab your favorite fruits, skewer them up, and enjoy this simple yet rewarding recipe. Happy holidays and happy snacking!</p>\n",
